for (int pos=0; pos<postingsFreqs.length; pos++) {
    Term[] terms = termArrays.get(pos);
```
```java
postingsFreqs[pos] = new PhraseQuery.PostingsAndFreq(postingsEnum, docFreq, positions.get(pos).intValue());
```
Reason:
The loop variable has been changed from `i` to `pos`, ensuring that the correct index is used consistently across all arrays. This prevents the AIOOBE by ensuring that the indexing is aligned with the actual size of the `termArrays` and `positions`, thus avoiding out-of-bounds access.

